          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in chromium-browser. An out-of-bounds write vulnerability in ANGLE, a component used for graphics rendering, could allow a remote attacker to execute malicious code. This vulnerability can be exploited by tricking a user into visiting a specially crafted web page. Successful exploitation could lead to arbitrary code execution, potentially allowing the attacker to take control of the affected system.",
